{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The dish is centered with generous negative space, captured at a 3/4 overhead angle to showcase all components. The foreground features one plate clearly, with a second identical serving plate softly blurred in the background. Shallow depth of field creates a natural bokeh. Lighting is soft natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the sheen of the puttanesca sauce. The setting is a rustic aged oak table with visible wood grain. Props include a wooden spoon resting casually beside the plates and a few scattered kalamata olive halves and a stray caper on the table surface. The dish features a base of fluffy, light-brown cooked quinoa. Tender turkey breast cutlets with golden-brown seared edges are nestled directly next to the quinoa, not covered by it. A chunky, rustic puttanesca sauce—rich with red tomato pieces, dark purple kalamata olive halves, and bright green capers—is spooned over the turkey. Diced zucchini, slightly softened and caramelized, are visible within the sauce. The dish is topped with fresh, vibrant green chopped basil. The scene is photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. It reflects a home-cooked, warm, and authentic meal. Includes slight natural imperfections like a small sauce drip on the rim and uneven browning on the turkey. Features a warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces."
}
